          "content": "## Unit 2 applied investigation\n\nYour group has been assigned a flood-bypass junction. Develop a falsifiable hydraulic model, list all inputs in a measurement register, show how mass conservation is checked and identify a second method of checking the primary output. Compare a low-flow, baseline and high-flow condition. Discuss surface roughness and seasonal temperature change as two possible sources of disagreement. Provide a table of calculated values, explain whether results are stable under small input changes, and separate teaching-model conclusions from claims requiring field verification.\n\n### Decision memo\n\nPrepare a two-page report containing the question, assumptions, data provenance, dimensional checks, one independent cross-check, sensitivity findings, limitations and a practical next measurement. Report uncertainty without inventing probabilities. Include a safe operating implication and identify exactly which engineering decision is not justified by the simplified model.\n\n### Review prompts\n\nExplain why conservation is not equivalent to assuming zero losses. Distinguish an ideal law, an empirical coefficient, an instrument reading and a numerical approximation. Explain how a model can generate a precise value yet still be inappropriate for a culvert, pump, gate or open-channel condition."
