          "content": "This unit addresses a linked set of civil-engineering decisions rather than a collection of disconnected equations. In a municipal overflow spillway, an analyst first asks which processes dominate, where the control boundaries belong, and which field evidence can discriminate between alternative explanations. The governing relation is useful only after each variable, units, sign convention and physical domain have been checked. A calculation is one element of a design argument, never a substitute for the argument itself."
