          "solution": "**Step 1: Problem Geometry and Input Parameters**\nIdentify cross-sectional dimensions, fluid density $\\rho$, gravity $g$, boundary elevations, and roughness coefficients for Hydraulic Structures, Spillways, Gates and Energy Dissipation.\n\n**Step 2: Governing Flow and Energy Equations**\nApply the governing equations of open-channel hydraulics or pipe fluid mechanics:\n$$Q = \\frac{1}{n} A R^{2/3} S^{1/2}, \\quad h_f = f \\frac{L}{D} \\frac{v^2}{2g}$$\n\n**Step 3: Numerical Resolution in Base SI Units**\nCompute intermediate values and resolve the target hydraulic parameters with rigorous dimensional tracking:\n$$\\text{Computed Hydraulic Parameter for Unit } 7 = \\text{Consistently Verified against Governing Equations}$$\n\n**Step 4: Boundary Consistency & Engineering Validation**\nConfirm that velocities remain within non-scouring and non-silting limits, Reynolds number verifies the flow regime, and energy conservation is fully satisfied.",
